      "sourceUnits": [
        {
          "id": "s0178",
          "zh": "后使黃門侍朗潘岳作書草，令小婢承福，以紙筆及草，因太子醉，稱詔使書之，文曰：「陛下宜自了，不自了，吾當入了之。",
          "en": "The empress had Pan Yue, Yellow Gate Attendant, draft a letter and sent the maid Cheng Fu with paper, brush, and draft. While the heir apparent was drunk she claimed an imperial order and made him copy it. The text read: \"Your Majesty ought to settle this yourself. If you do not, I shall enter and settle it.",
          "literal": "The empress had the Yellow Gate Attendant Pan Yue draft a letter, ordered the little maid Cheng Fu to bring paper, brush, and draft; taking advantage of the Heir Apparent's drunkenness she claimed an edict and made him write it. The text read: \"Your Majesty ought to settle matters yourself; if you do not settle them, I shall enter and settle them.",
          "blockIndex": 25
        }
      ]
